# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Shell scripts and YAML configs must stay LF on every OS. A YAML saved with
# Windows/CRLF line endings injects a stray carriage return (\r) into the
# values that docker_setup/*.sh parse for `output_dir` / `synthpop_dir`, which
# makes `docker run --mount` fail with "value should not have whitespace".
# (The scripts also strip \r defensively, but keeping tracked files LF avoids
# the problem at the source.)
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.R    text eol=lf
# PowerShell runs fine with LF (PowerShell 5.1+ and pwsh); the repo stores these
# LF already, so keep them LF to avoid CRLF churn and the very mixed-ending
# problems this file exists to prevent.
*.ps1  text eol=lf
